,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59117479?"},"repo":{"id":1423101235,"name":"Gathin23/cleanyourtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv"},"payload":{"action":"started"},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T05:59:30Z"},{"id":"17782011689","type":"WatchEvent","actor":{"id":34831532,"login":"jylc","display_login":"jylc","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jylc","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34831532?"},"repo":{"id":1423101235,"name":"Gathin23/cleanyourtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv"},"payload":{"action":"started"},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T05:59:27Z"},{"id":"17782011445","type":"WatchEvent","actor":{"id":32301686,"login":"liuhuan-infra","display_login":"liuhuan-infra","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuhuan-infra","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32301686?"},"repo":{"id":1423101235,"name":"Gathin23/cleanyourtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv"},"payload":{"action":"started"},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T05:59:26Z"},{"id":"17782011282","type":"WatchEvent","actor":{"id":26090203,"login":"jingjingxinshang","display_login":"jingjingxinshang","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jingjingxinshang","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26090203?"},"repo":{"id":1423101235,"name":"Gathin23/cleanyourtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv"},"payload":{"action":"started"},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T05:59:27Z"},{"id":"17782006015","type":"IssueCommentEvent","actor":{"id":56357338,"login":"xbsheng","display_login":"xbsheng","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56357338?"},"repo":{"id":1423101235,"name":"Gathin23/cleanyourtv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv"},"payload":{"action":"created","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/442","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/442/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/442/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/442/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/pull/442","id":5947029060,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVNLNM88AAAABJnZvPA","number":442,"title":"docs: the China TCL verifier gate can be stepped around for one install (#376)","user":{"login":"xbsheng","id":56357338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MzU3MzM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56357338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xbsheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-20T18:12:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T05:31:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/pulls/442","html_url":"https://github.com/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/pull/442","diff_url":"https://github.com/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/pull/442.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/pull/442.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"**What this changes:** the three places that say a third-party launcher can never be installed on China TCL / FFalcon firmware now point at the workaround in #376, and `docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md` has the recipe with its caveats. Docs only, no code, no list entries.\n\n**Tested on:** no TV — I have none of these sets. Everything factual here is the report in #376 from a FFalcon 75R685C owner (`tcl_mt5879_cn`, Android 11, `RQ3A.210705.001`), transcribed with the unit named, plus the `murilocb` comment there for the G03 app-ops line. Unit tests only (`CLEANYOURTV_STRICT=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`, 56/56).\n\n### Why\n\nThe repo currently concludes \"impossible, stop retrying\":\n\n- `PROMPT.md` — \"say plainly that the launcher half is impossible here, and stop retrying installs\";\n- `README.md` Supported TVs — \"refuse to install any launcher at all\";\n- `examples/tcl-q10g-pro/debloat.txt` — \"A third-party launcher cannot be installed here\".\n\nThat is right for a bare `adb install` / `pm install`, which is all any of those notes describe. It is not right in general: the refusal comes from the verifier in front of `pm install` (`com.android.packageinstaller` → verifier/InstallStrategyManager → LauncherStrategy, the gate the q10g-pro header already documents). Taking the verifier process out of the loop for the length of one install lets even an APK declaring `MAIN`+`HOME` through — `Success`, with `pm list packages -d` showing packageinstaller enabled again afterwards and a full `reboot` back to normal on that unit.\n\n### Trade-offs\n\n- **Presented as a fallback, not a default.** The window leaves a TV that can install and uninstall nothing while it is open, so the bullet says the re-enable is not optional, belongs in the same script with nothing in between, and an interrupted window has to be closed with `pm enable` over ADB. Nothing is patched and no property is changed; only the verifier is skipped.\n- **Installing is not owning Home.** On this family the firmware still boots `com.tcl.cyberui` until the two TCL-only app ops are allowed, so the bullet says that too rather than letting \"it installed\" read as \"it works\".\n- **The q10g-pro note is scoped, not overwritten.** It was seen on the sibling 75R685C on the same `tcl_mt5879_cn` platform and not on the 55Q10G Pro itself, so the header says exactly that and the existing gate description stays.\n- **`tcl-ak30a5` and `examples/README.md` are untouched**: that Android 9 set's refusal is a different gate and nobody has tried the window on it.\n- **Commands are written for `tools/tv.py`**, the convention that file's header documents; they are the same three shell commands the report gives as `adb shell` lines.\n\n### Tests\n\n`tests/test_docs_install_window.py` (6 tests) pins the order of the three commands inside the window (disable → install → enable, so the window cannot be documented backwards and strand a TV), the \"not optional\" wording, the named scope, and the three pointers. All 6 fail on the current `main` (checked by stashing the doc changes: 6 failures) and pass with them.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/442/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/442/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},"comment":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/comments/6308841603","html_url":"https://github.com/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/pull/442#issuecomment-6308841603","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/442","id":6308841603,"node_id":"IC_kwDOVNLNM88AAAABeAlIgw","user":{"login":"xbsheng","id":56357338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MzU3MzM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56357338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xbsheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xbsheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T05:31:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T05:31:36Z","body":"Rebased onto `9071ec8` (Launcher 2.5). No file-level conflict, but main had landed the Samsung Tizen note in the same \"Supported TVs\" paragraph, so I merged the two: the Tizen pointer stays, and the absolute \"refuse to install any launcher at all\" becomes the verifier window that #376 actually measured — `Some China-market TCL sets refuse sideloads, launcher or not, until the verifier in front of pm install is stepped aside for one install; docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md has that window.`\n\nRe-verified on the new base: `CLEANYOURTV_STRICT=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` 126 tests OK, `bash -n` clean on every `tools/*.sh` and `launcher/*.sh`, both CI jobs green on e81d46d.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/comments/6308841603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-10-21T05:31:36Z"},{"id":"17781989201","type":"WatchEvent","actor":{"id":3993633,"login":"n0smi1e","display_login":"n0smi1e","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/n0smi1e","avatar